    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2080" root="بذخ" body-key="b">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِذِخْ</span></b>  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَذَخْ</span> [for the latter of which, in the
CK, we find <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَذِخْ</span>,] <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَخْ</span> [<i>Excellent!</i> &amp;c.];
(JK, T, K, TA;) and <i>wonderful!</i> (T, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِذِخْ بِذِخْ</span> is also said in chiding a camel that
brays in the most vehement manner, (see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَذَخَ</span>,)
or in imitating his braying. (L.)

